e BUILT' (config.py:197-201)"],"finding":"The Bedrock-availability mechanism can only assert provider IDENTITY, not credential USABILITY: available_backends() exposes no Bedrock/AWS-credential signal, and Bedrock authenticates through the ambient AWS chain with no rebar-managed key (config.py:362-364). So 'recognize the configured/inferred Bedrock provider as live' reports live-available whenever the resolved model string is Bedrock-qualified — even in an environment with zero resolvable AWS credentials. The plan phrase 'relying on rebar's existing Bedrock region/ambient AWS credential chain' overstates what is actually checked (the chain is not probed; only the provider name is). The plan should state that this is availability-by-configuration (provider selected), not usability (creds present), and confirm the new --require-live fail-on-zero-success path is the intended safety net for the false-positive-live Bedrock case.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6e5b8cc045d9b860","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan', bullet: 'Update _live_criteria_eval_available to recognize the configured/inferred Bedrock provider as live ... relying on rebar's existing Bedrock region/ambient AWS credential chain'","norm_id":"n63f0d82184424834","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Bedrock-configured repo with NO AWS credentials runs `criteria eval --changed-since ... --require-live`: now reported live-available, attempts calibrate_criterion, every criterion raises LLMError"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the Bedrock live-availability decision rule: name the provider source (explicit `model_provider` / `split_provider_qualifier` / `infer_provider`), which qualifier values count (`bedrock`, `gateway/bedrock`), and the concrete 'available' predicate (e.g. a new `available_backends()` Bedrock key vs region/credential-chain probe).","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'recognize the configured/inferred Bedrock provider as live when the agents runtime is installed, relying on rebar's existing Bedrock region/ambient AWS credential chain instead of Anthropic/OpenAI key checks'","available_backends() returns only {'pydantic_ai','anthropic_api_key','openai_api_key','langfuse_configured','tracing_extra'} — no Bedrock detection exists to build on","KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES holds BOTH 'bedrock' and 'gateway/bedrock'; the plan does not say which qualifies, nor how provider is obtained (model_provider vs split_provider_qualifier vs infer_provider)"],"finding":"The plan's proposed Bedrock live-availability rule references an 'inferred Bedrock provider' and 'existing Bedrock region/ambient AWS credential chain' but never defines the detection vocabulary or predicate an executor needs: (a) which provider signal counts as Bedrock — explicit `model_provider`, the `infer_provider(model)` result, and/or the `bedrock` vs `gateway/bedrock` qualifier in KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES — and (b) what 'available' means for the AWS credential chain (region presence alone, boto3 credential resolution, or a new `available_backends()` key). `available_backends()` currently exposes no Bedrock key at all.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8576a514f02696ff","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan → Plan bullet 2 ('Update _live_criteria_eval_available to recognize the configured/inferred Bedrock provider as live'); src/rebar/llm/config.py:525 (available_backends), :202 (KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES), :253 (infer_provider)","norm_id":"ne5c2940fc4b2d48a","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Bedrock-configured repo with only AWS ambient creds and region set","Repo using a `gateway/bedrock:...` model string","Repo with a bare Bedrock model id and no explicit provider (infer_provider path)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that availability is true when agents runtime is installed AND `infer_provider(resolve_model(...))` (or explicit `model_provider`) resolves to `bedrock`/`gateway/bedrock`, gated on a specific ambient-credential check (e.g. a new `available_backends()['bedrock']` derived from boto3 credential resolution and/or REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION).","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the concrete side-effect-free detection API `_live_criteria_eval_available` will use to identify a configured/inferred Bedrock provider (e.g. resolve the configured model string's provider + ProviderSession.is_resolvable('bedrock') / bedrock_provider extra check), and state whether `available_backends()` must gain a Bedrock key, since it currently exposes none.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.23,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["available_backends() returns only pydantic_ai / anthropic_api_key / openai_api_key / langfuse_configured / tracing_extra (src/rebar/llm/config.py:529-539) — no bedrock/provider-resolution key","bedrock_model.py:137 raises when the optional bedrock provider package is not installed; bedrock_model.py:161 raises when no AWS region resolves — both are separate from the `agents` extra","Plan text: 'relying on rebar's existing Bedrock region/ambient AWS credential chain instead of Anthropic/OpenAI key checks' names a chain but not the concrete detect-without-constructing API"],"finding":"The plan asserts `_live_criteria_eval_available` can 'recognize the configured/inferred Bedrock provider as live when the agents runtime is installed' but does not name the detection API. The existing `available_backends()` snapshot (config.py:525) surfaces no Bedrock/provider key, and Bedrock requires a separate `bedrock_provider` optional package plus a resolvable AWS region (bedrock_model.py:137,161) — so 'agents installed' alone does not establish live-availability.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f03ebd466e7f9125e","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' — 'Update `_live_criteria_eval_available` to recognize the configured/inferred Bedrock provider as live'","norm_id":"n69eff4002adb21da","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Bedrock-only environment where the agents extra is installed but the bedrock_provider package is absent or no region resolves — the new gate could report live-available and then the run fails inside calibrate_criterion","Determining whether the configured model string resolves to the bedrock provider without importing botocore/boto3 at detection time"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the per-criterion LLMError disposition explicitly: whether an LLMError is fatal-to-that-criterion vs retryable, and confirm that --require-live's zero-success non-zero exit does not mask an underlying retryable/transient (throttle) condition.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.834,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'when live is available but every criterion raises LLMError, the run returns None and the caller exits 0 unconditionally, even under --require-live'","'Have the live selected-criteria loop return a success count so --require-live can fail when live execution was attempted but produced zero successful evaluations.'","Absence: no disposition word (retryable/transient vs fatal/permanent) is attached to the LLMError arm; --require-live turning all-LLMError into a hard non-zero exit could mask a retryable primary throttle."],"finding":"The plan alters how per-criterion LLMError is handled (loop now returns a success count; --require-live fails non-zero on zero successes) but does not state, using explicit disposition words, whether an LLMError against one criterion is treated as fatal-to-that-criterion vs a transient/retryable condition — so it is unclear whether a retryable throttle (e.g. a Bedrock 429) surfaced as LLMError would be masked as a permanent zero-success failure under --require-live.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f85e92004003e7746","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section: 'Have the live selected-criteria loop return a success count so --require-live can fail...' and Deferred item 'per-criterion LLMError recovery path'","norm_id":"n4f8a72e6bbbb4085","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Under --require-live, every selected criterion raises an LLMError that is actually a transient Bedrock/Anthropic throttle; the run reports zero successes and exits non-zero as a permanent failure, obscuring that a retry would have succeeded."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":